course: dictionary
lesson: 7682
title: Protection: keeping safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Protection means keeping someone or something safe from harm, danger or damage. It can also be a thing that does the keeping safe, like a helmet or sun cream. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «A boy practised the drums without ear protection; after a few months he had ringing in his ears.» The clue is the ringing ears. Ear protection would have guarded his ears from the harm of loud noise, so it is a thing that keeps you safe.
explain: Protection can also mean the care that laws or people give to something, like the protection of wild animals. To check your meaning, swap in "keeping safe" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Protection means keeping someone or something safe from harm, danger or damage.
fact: Protection often comes with a word after it, such as «protection from» or «protection against»: «protection from pain and illness».
fact: «Sun protection» means things like a hat, sun cream and shade that keep the sun from harming your skin.
fact: Animals have protection too: shells, spines and camouflage help keep them safe in nature.
fact: The simplest protection against germs is washing your hands with soap and warm water for about 20 seconds.
exercise: «Sun cream should be at least SPF 30 with good UVA protection.» What does protection mean in this sentence? | A sweet taste you can smell | *Keeping your skin safe from the sun's harm | Being sent indoors to rest | A loud noise that scares birds
exercise: Which of these is a protection you wear to keep your head safe? | *A helmet | A bike bell | A puddle | A bike chain
exercise: «Animals have protection like shells, spines and camouflage.» Find and copy one thing that gives animals protection. | *shells | science | nature — hmm | camouflage is not here
test: «It is so loud that workers wear ear protection.» Why do the workers wear ear protection? | *To keep their ears safe from the loud noise | To help them sleep at night | To look fashionable at work | To make the noise louder
test: «Every pet needs protection from pain and illness.» Which phrase tells you what the protection is against? | company or the right to live alone | fresh water | *from pain and illness | a good home
exam: Which phrase means the care that laws or people give to something? | sun cream | a helmet | *the protection of wild animals | ear protection
